  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-05-28T18:50:51.857Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Though there is one other post I've found with this proposition, its activity is very small.  As a PC user with a lot of friends using Quest, searching for worlds to hang out in quickly becomes exhausting when I have to sort through looking at the small dots in the corners to tell if we can all visit or not.\nA simple enough solution to this would be adding a toggle (similar to the \"show community labs\" toggle) to exclusively show cross-platform worlds (in search results at minimum, but ideally in the quick-menus like the Hot section as well).  My current work-around is to save a search for worlds with the author tag for Quest, but since the search saves only allow three queries total, it would be a lot nicer if this wasn't using up a limited resource.",
